# {{.ProjectName}} Vue.js Frontend

A Vue.js frontend application for {{.ProjectName}}.

## Features

- Vue 3 with Composition API support
- Vue Router for single-page application routing
- Vue CLI for development and build tooling
- Modern JavaScript (ES6+) support
- CSS scoped styling
- Hot reload development server
- Production-optimized builds
- Docker support with Nginx

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+
- npm

### Local Development

1. Install dependencies:
```bash
npm install
```

2. Start the development server:
```bash
npm run serve
```

The application will be available at http://localhost:8080

### Production Build

```bash
npm run build
```

### Docker Development

1. Build the Docker image:
```bash
docker build -t {{.ProjectName}}-frontend .
```

2. Run the container:
```bash
docker run -p 80:80 {{.ProjectName}}-frontend
```

## Available Scripts

- `npm run serve` - Start development server with hot reload
- `npm run build` - Create production build
- `npm run test:unit` - Run unit tests
- `npm run lint` - Lint and fix files

## Project Structure

```
.
├── public/
│   ├── index.html      # HTML template
│   └── favicon.ico     # App icon
├── src/
│   ├── App.vue         # Main App component
│   ├── main.js         # Application entry point
│   ├── router/
│   │   └── index.js    # Router configuration
│   └── views/
│       └── HomeView.vue # Home page component
├── package.json        # Dependencies and scripts
├── Dockerfile         # Docker configuration
├── nginx.conf         # Nginx configuration for production
├── .gitignore        # Git ignore rules
└── README.md         # This file
```

## Customization

- Modify `src/App.vue` to update the main application layout
- Add new views in the `src/views/` directory
- Create reusable components in the `src/components/` directory
- Update routes in `src/router/index.js`
- Configure API endpoints to connect with your backend service